    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">5% GST for interstate transport:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">If your bike transport involves moving the bike between two different Indian states, the tax rate may be reduced to 5%. This reduced rate is applicable for interstate transport, which includes Eluru and Hyderabad being in different states.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<p>Insurance is crucial for protecting both you and the transport service provider in case of any damages or incidents during transit. In India, you'll need to consider two types of insurance:</p>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Declared Value Insurance:</strong> Also known as "Declared Value Transit Marine Insurance," this type of insurance covers your bike against any damages or theft during transit. You, as the bike owner, declare the declared value for the insurance coverage.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Actual Value Insurance:</strong> Actual Value Insurance covers your bike based on its actual value, taking into account its make, model, and age. This type of insurance is more comprehensive and protects you better than Declared Value Insurance.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Declared Value Insurance:</h3>
	<p>For Declared Value Insurance, the premium rates depend on the declared value of your bike. The premium will be calculated as a percentage of the declared value. The insurance company will provide you with a quotation based on the declared value. Some factors that may affect the percentage include:</p></div>
